    "short_description": {
        "value": "TESSERA is a pixel-wise, multi-modal (Sentinel-1/2) remote sensing foundation model that learns robust, label-efficient embeddings from irregular, sparse EO time series. It uses Barlow Twins self-supervised learning, global shuffling, and mix-based regularization to produce global, annual, 10m, int8 embeddings for every land pixel, enabling state-of-the-art performance on classification, segmentation, and regression tasks with minimal computation and high label efficiency.",
        "confidence": 0.7533
    },
